2026-09-24 — causal diagnosis of the frozen vmaccess attach deadlock.

Small C: ptrace-exec-reap-cycle.c. The child creates a PTRACE_TRACEME sibling,
joins it, and enters exec. The parent enters PTRACE_ATTACH without first
reaping that sibling. A second parent thread observes both kernel stacks,
then performs exactly that waitpid. Both retained kernels show:
  tracer stack contains ptrace_attach;
  tracee stack contains begin_new_exec (EvoCC also shows de_thread);
  sibling waitpid reports its successful exit;
  the blocked PTRACE_ATTACH then returns 0, not EAGAIN;
  the stop/detach/kill/reap cleanup completes with no children left.
Both bounded reductions PASS and shut down. This is an active causal
intervention, not merely “both kernels time out” or a timing-only retry.

Frozen kernel/ptrace.c:457 takes cred_guard_mutex with mutex_intr, returning
ERESTARTNOINTR on interruption. Frozen fs/exec.c takes that mutex before
begin_new_exec/de_thread; de_thread waits for traced siblings to be reaped.
The original single tracer cannot reap while blocked trying to attach.
This identifies the frozen kernel/test contract mismatch independently of
EvoCC: the test expects a nonblocking EAGAIN which this kernel path lacks.
Updating that source/API/test baseline is separate authority, not a compiler
repair, timeout extension, or permission to fabricate a PASS.

Fresh unchanged ptrace:vmaccess on both Images: 1 PASS / 1 FAIL (the original
30-second attach-subtest timeout), program FAIL. Both 45-second wrapper and
nonce-bound boot/shutdown remain unchanged and complete. No original source,
assertion, userspace binary, kernel or config was edited. All snapshot disk
hashes are unchanged. K11d closes causal classification only; K11/K13 remain.

Probe compiles with sealed GCC-14 -static -pthread -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror,
zero compilation errors; uses a ten-second safety alarm and fifteen-second
outer bound. The ordinary runtime init is reused. Changed gate b10a00d selects
no Rust crate; diff checks pass. All diagnostic children and VMs are reaped.
Artifacts total 2.3 MiB; no Image or test disk copies.

